    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d134">

                <pb facs="d133-03" n="3" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76ve05p1/d133-03"/>

                <head>134. Memorandum From the Executive Secretary of the Department of State
                    (Eliot) to the Presidentʼs Assistant for National Security Affairs
                        (Kissinger)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d134-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d134-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1969-11-01"
                        >November 1, 1969</date>
                </dateline>
                <pb facs="d134-01" n="1" xml:id="d134-01"/>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>Subject:</label>
                    <item>Proposed Presidential Statement On Biafran Relief</item>
                </list>
                <p>On instruction from Under Secretary Richardson I am enclosing a proposed
                    Presidential Statement on the impasse of Red Cross relief to Biafra. This draft
                    is the result of extensive discussions with the NSC staff.</p>
                <p>The Under Secretary recommends that the statement be released early next
                    week.</p>
                <closer><signed>Theodore L. Eliot, Jr.</signed>Executive Secretary</closer>


                <xi:include href="d134-a1.xml" xpointer="d134-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d134-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d134-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, Central Files 1967–69, POL 27–9 Biafra-Nigeria.
                    No classification marking. The statement was not released. See <ref
                        target="#d135">Document 135</ref>, Attachment C thereto, and <ref
                        target="#d137">Document 137</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d134-f2" n="2" xml:id="d134-f2-content">
                <p>Under Secretary of State Elliot Richardson proposed a Presidential statement that
                    placed responsibility on Biafran authorities for the failure to achieve an
                    agreement for daytime International Committee of the Red Cross (ICRC) relief
                    flights. Robert L. Brown signed the memorandum for Eliot.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
